    skos:editorialNote "This concept is a proposed-mechanism category in an evidence model, not the cognitive phenomenon itself, so relatedMatch is intentionally weaker than exactMatch."@en .


###########################################################################
# OBO Foundry class alignments
###########################################################################
#
# The rationale below is kept even where the axiom is now a comment: it is why
# the mapping is what it is, and it is not recorded anywhere else. Each axiom is
# asserted once, in the module that defines the class, following the convention
# this file already used for sstim:SessionInstance -> prov:Activity.

# Sensory stimulation intervention → planned process.
# OBI_0000011 is obsolete and must not appear in live logical axioms. SSTIM
# uses the active, broader COB_0000082 'planned process' term because an
# intervention need not be completely executed (verified via OLS, 2026-07-10).
# sstim:SensoryStimulationIntervention rdfs:subClassOf cob:0000082 .
#   Asserted in sstim-session.ttl; commented here so the Full closure does
#   not carry the axiom twice.

# Technique → information content entity. OBI_0000272 requires enough detail
# for independent process reproduction; a reusable technique category is less
# specific and is therefore not an OBI protocol (ADR 0014 review disposition).
# sstim:SensoryStimulationTechnique rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030 .
#   Asserted in sstim-technique.ttl; commented here to avoid a duplicate.

# Protocol → OBI protocol. A preset is an information content entity that FOLLOWS
# a protocol via sstim:followsProtocol; it is not itself a protocol (see ADR 0014).
# sstim:SensoryStimulationProtocol rdfs:subClassOf obi:0000272 .
#   Asserted in sstim-technique.ttl; commented here to avoid a duplicate.

# Session instance → PROV Activity (stated in sstim-session.ttl; repeated here
# for cross-reference in alignment context)
# sstim:SessionInstance rdfs:subClassOf prov:Activity .

# Evidence claim → IAO information content entity.
# (Was iao:0000001 'conditional specification' — wrong; an evidence claim is
# not a conditional specification. iao:0000030 is the correct generalization.)
# sstim:EvidenceClaim rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030 .
#   Asserted in sstim-evidence.ttl; commented here to avoid a duplicate.

# Frequency band → IAO information content entity
# sstim:FrequencyBand rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030 .
#   Asserted in sstim-common.ttl, which reaches Core Plus; alignments is
#   Full-only, so asserting it here as well would add a duplicate triple
#   without widening the profile that carries the parent.

# Reference → IAO document
sstim:PublicSafeReference rdfs:subClassOf iao:0000030 .

# SSTIM controlled-value classes (including SensoryModality,
# StimulationMechanism, and IntendedEffect) are information categories, not
# the real-world roles, processes, or dispositions they classify (ADR 0021).

# ECO (Evidence & Conclusion Ontology) classifies evidence by TYPE / provenance,
# not by strength, so it has no clean match for the SSTIM evidence-tier concepts
# (speculative…established), which are GRADE-style strength grades. The former
# `sstim-v:tierEstablished skos:closeMatch eco:0006151` mapping was removed:
# ECO_0006151 is "documented statement evidence", not a systematic review, and
# ECO has no review/meta-analysis strength term. Left unmapped intentionally.


###########################################################################
# External upper-ontology term labels (display stubs)
#
# Local rdfs:label assertions for the external BFO/OBI/IAO IRIs referenced
# above and across the semantic dependency modules, so the knowledge browser
# renders readable
# names instead of opaque numeric IRIs. These are display aids, not
# authoritative definitions — the canonical labels live in BFO/OBI/IAO.
###########################################################################

bfo:0000015 rdfs:label "process"@en .
bfo:0000016 rdfs:label "disposition"@en .
obi:0000272 rdfs:label "protocol"@en .
cob:0000082 rdfs:label "planned process"@en .
iao:0000030 rdfs:label "information content entity"@en .


###########################################################################
